+## 7. Work left for the next release (Rails 7.0 on framework defaults)
+
+Next will run Ruby 3.2 + Rails 7.0.x with `config.load_defaults 7.0` in
+`config/application.rb`. To stay rollback-safe to **this** release (6.1/hybrid/SHA1+SHA256):
+
+### Must do in next release (before or with `load_defaults 7.0`)
+
+- [ ] **Add `config.load_defaults 7.0`** (replaces no-`load_defaults`).
+  Audit every default in `new_framework_defaults_7_0.rb.tt` and Rails guide.
+  Most are safe (see below), but these need explicit handling:
+- [ ] **Keep `cookies_serializer = :hybrid` temporarily, not pure `:json`.**
+  `load_defaults 7.0` sets `:json`, which cannot read pre-hybrid Marshal cookies.
+  This release already writes JSON via hybrid and auto-migrates on read, but
+  long-lived browsers could still hold Marshal cookies from *before* this release
+  if next ships too soon after this. Keep `config.action_dispatch.cookies_serializer = :hybrid`
+  explicitly **after** `load_defaults 7.0` until confident all Marshal cookies gone
+  (e.g. 2× max session lifetime + deploy window; sessions are browser-close,
+  but allow 30 days to match mail-link window for safety). Then delete line to
+  inherit `:json`. Monitor for `MARSHAL_SIGNATURE` reads.
+- [ ] **Keep `40-upgrade-rotations.rb` (SHA1+SHA256) initially.**
+  `load_defaults 7.0` makes primary SHA256; without SHA1 fallback, this release's
+  SHA1 sessions/mail links invalidate on upgrade (sign-out + broken links).
+  Our file already adds both, so keeping it makes next's SHA256 primary read
+  this release's SHA1. **Do not delete in next release.** Delete only after
+  SHA1 expiry window (30 days for mail links + session window after last SHA1
+  deploy). See §5 table.
+- [ ] **Pin `cache_format_version = 6.1` after `load_defaults 7.0`.**
+  `load_defaults` sets `7.0`, unreadable by this 6.1 rollback target.
+  Add `config.active_support.cache_format_version = 6.1` explicitly after
+  `load_defaults` with comment. Bump to `7.0` only after fully on 7.0 with
+  **no rollback planned** (separate later release). Cache miss (not sign-out)
+  is the risk, but pin avoids even that.
+- [ ] **Verify `use_authenticated_cookie_encryption` / `use_cookies_with_metadata` flip.**
+  `load_defaults` flips `false`→`true`. Verified safe via automatic rotations
+  + our digest rotations (see §3, §6). No extra code, but add monitoring for
+  `InvalidMessage` / `InvalidSignature` spikes on deploy/rollback.
+- [ ] **Verify `hash_digest_class = SHA256` (was `MD5`).**
+  Invalidates `ActiveSupport::Digest` cache keys/ETags (cache miss, not sign-out).
+  No code change, but expect cold cache on deploy/rollback. Consider warming.
+- [ ] **Keep `legacy_connection_handling = false` (now redundant).**
+  `load_defaults` sets it; our explicit line becomes no-op. Can delete or keep.
+- [ ] **Keep `Mime::Type.register_alias :api` and `Resolver#find_all` branch.**
+  Both required on 7.0 (see §4). Do not delete. After 6.1 retired, simplify
