+## 9. Rollback drill (ops)
+
+- **This (6.1/hybrid/SHA1+SHA256) → Previous (6.1/marshal/SHA1):**
+  Safe. This writes JSON (readable by prev via fallback) + SHA1 primary (readable by prev).
+  SHA256 fallback values (from future, if this had read them) are **not** written by this
+  (this writes SHA1 primary), so prev never sees SHA256. No action.
+- **Next (7.0/json/SHA256+SHA1-fallback) → This (6.1/hybrid/SHA1+SHA256-fallback):**
+  Safe. Next writes JSON/GCM/SHA256/with-purpose; this reads via hybrid (JSON) +
+  GCM/SHA256 rotation + purpose fallback. Mail links: next writes SHA256, this verifies
+  via SHA256 rotation. No action, but keep this release's code deployed as rollback target
+  (do not delete rotations/hybrid before next is stable).
+- **Cache:** Expect miss on every deploy/rollback until `cache_format_version` stabilized
+  on `7.0` (after no-rollback). Not a sign-out.
+- **Monitoring:** Watch `InvalidSignature` / `InvalidMessage` (cookies/verifiers),
+  `UnknownFormat` (API resolver), session creation rate (sign-out spike would show as
+  mass re-logins), and `mail_links/unwatch` 404 rate (broken-link spike).
